{
  "dom_id": "step-q124540",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "What is $\\operatorname{cos}⁡{640}^{∘}$ expressed in terms of a reference angle?",
  "worked_solution": "We wish to express $\\operatorname{cos}⁡{640}^{∘}$ in terms of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡{\\theta }_{R},$ where ${\\theta }_{R}$ is the reference angle corresponding to the angle $\\theta ={640}^{∘}.$\n\nTo express $\\operatorname{cos}⁡{640}^{∘}$ in terms of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡{\\theta }_{R},$ we proceed as follows:\n\n- **Step 1**: Find the corresponding coterminal angle that lies in the range $[{0}^{∘},{360}^{∘}).$ We do this by subtracting integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ until we get our desired angle.\n\n$$\n{640}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}={280}^{∘}\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡{640}^{∘}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{280}^{∘}.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14253971/assets/664e1c8c7becf7a8e53cbf0c1a7c5dc02ec136b5ff59d6186a589b001ba6eb3c.png)\n\n- **Step 2**: Compute the reference angle. Since $\\theta ={280}^{∘}$ is in the $4$th quadrant, the reference angle is\n\n$$\n{\\theta }_{R}={360}^{∘}-{280}^{∘}={80}^{∘}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 3**: Determine the correct sign. The cosine function is positive $(+)$ in the fourth quadrant. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡{640}^{∘}=+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{\\theta }_{R}=+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{80}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡{640}^{∘}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{80}^{∘}.\n$$",
